            { t:"Hiroo Kanamori contributed to the moment magnitude scale, but the account uses one station without calibration, travel-time comparison, or site response. The source estimate is incomplete.", v:"partial", fb:"This offers part of the analysis but leaves source, path, site, or network uncertainty open." },
            { t:"Hiroo Kanamori is portrayed as proving that every unusual seismic arrival indicates a separate underground explosion. The waveform says otherwise. The focal mechanism points in another direction.", v:"wrong", fb:"That conclusion is inconsistent with how seismic waves or hazard models are interpreted." },
            { t:"Hiroo Kanamori is invoked to defund warning because exact long-range earthquake prediction remains unreliable. Warning seconds are discarded. Prediction limits are misused to abandon detection.", v:"danger", fb:"That choice treats incomplete prediction as a reason to discard monitoring and rapid warning." }
